                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2766666,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "In terms of production, this means that you only use what you need, and so there wouldn't be any waste. The notion that you could create anything at all has major implications for our health. It means that we'll eventually be able to replicate anything. This would have a phenomenal effect on our society. In time, it could even lead to the eradication of famine through the introduction of machines that produce food to feed the hungry.",
            "children": [
              {
